rait.jpg","gender":"M","born":"1941-10-10","died":"2022-07-06","birthplace":"Lelu","parties":["independent politician"],"education":["University of Guam","University of Hawaiʻi System","Bailey Olter High School"],"occupations":["politician"],"wiki":"Jacob Nena"},"Q448296":{"id":"Q448296","name":"Leo Falcam","desc":"President of Federated States of Micronesia (1935-2018)","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Leo_Falcam.jpg/330px-Leo_Falcam.jpg","gender":"M","born":"1935-11-20","died":"2018-02-12","birthplace":"U","parties":[],"education":["University of Hawaiʻi System","Princeton University"],"occupations":["politician","governor"],"wiki":"Leo Falcam"},"Q435427":{"id":"Q435427","name":"Joseph Urusemal","desc":"President of Micronesia","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Joseph_Urusemal.jpg/330px-Joseph_Urusemal.jpg","gender":"M","born":"1952-03-19","died":"2025-09-16","birthplace":"Woleai","parties":[],"education":["Rockhurst University","Xavier High School, Micronesia"],"occupations":["politician"],"wiki":"Joseph Urusemal"},"Q57499":{"id":"Q57499","name":"Manny Mori","desc":"President of the Federated States of Micronesia","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/MoriFSM.jpg/330px-MoriFSM.jpg","gender":"M","born":"1948-12-25","died":null,"birthplace":"Fefan","parties":["independent politician"],"education":["University of Guam","Xavier High School, Micronesia"],"occupations":["politician"],"wiki":"Manny Mori"},"Q19921375":{"id":"Q19921375","name":"Peter M. Christian","desc":"President of the Federated States of Micronesia","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/President_Peter_M._Christian.jpg/330px-President_Peter_M._Christian.jpg","gender":"M","born":"1947-10-16","died":null,"birthplace":"Pohnpei","parties":["independent politician"],"education":["University of Hawaiʻi at Mānoa","University of Guam","Xavier High School, Micronesia"],"occupations":["politician"],"wiki":"Peter M. Christian"},"Q63872093":{"id":"Q63872093","name":"David W. Panuelo","desc":"President of the Federated States of Micronesia (2019-present)","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/David_W._Panuelo_9th_President_of_the_FSM.jpg/330px-David_W._Panuelo_9th_President_of_the_FSM.jpg","gender":"M","born":"1964-04-13","died":null,"birthplace":"Pohnpei","parties":["independent politician"],"education":["Eastern Oregon University"],"occupations":["politician"],"wiki":"David Panuelo"},"Q7984081":{"id":"Q7984081","name":"Wesley Simina","desc":"Federated States of Micronesia politician","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Wesley_Simina%2C_Federated_States_of_Micronesia_President%2C_at_the_Department_of_State_in_Washington%2C_D.C._on_March_18%2C_2024_(cropped).jpg/330px-Wesley_Simina%2C_Federated_States_of_Micronesia_President%2C_at_the_Department_of_State_in_Washington%2C_D.C._on_March_18%2C_2024_(cropped).jpg","gender":"M","born":"1961-09-10","died":null,"birthplace":null,"parties":[],"education":["University of Hawaiʻi System"],"occupations":["politician"],"wiki":"Wesley Simina"}},"summary":"The Federated States of Micronesia (FSM), or simply Micronesia ( ), is an island country in Micronesia, a region of Oceania. The federation encompasses the majority of the Caroline Islands (excluding Palau) and consists of four states—from west to east: Yap, Chuuk, Pohnpei, and Kosrae—that span the western Pacific just north of the equator for a longitudinal distance of almost 2,700 km (1,700 mi). Together, the states comprise around 607 islands and a combined land area of approximately 702 km2 or 271 sq mi.\nThe entire island federation lies across the northern Pacific accordingly: northeast of Indonesia and Papua New Guinea, south of Guam and the Marianas, west of Nauru and the Marshall Islands, east of Palau and the Philippines, about 2,900 km (1,800 mi) north of eastern Australia, 3,400 km (2,100 mi) southeast of Japan, and some 4,000 km (2,485 mi) southwest of Honolulu of the Hawaiian Islands.\nThe country's total land area is relatively small, but its waters occupy nearly 3 million km2 (1.2 million mi2) of the Pacific Ocean, giving the country the 14th-largest exclusive economic zone in the world. The nation's capital is Palikir, on Pohnpei Island, and its largest city is Weno, an island municipality in the Chuuk Lagoon.\nEach of its four states is centered on one or more main volcanic islands, and all but Kosrae include numerous outlying atolls. The FSM spreads across part of the Caroline Islands in the wider region of Micronesia, which region consists of thousands of small islands divided among several countries. The term Micronesia may refer to the Federated States of Micronesia or to the region as a whole.\nThe FSM was a part of the former Trust Territory of the Pacific Islands (TTPI), a United Nations Trust Territory administered by the United States from 1947 to 1994. On May 10, 1979, the islands ratified a constitutional government and then became a sovereign state after attaining independence on November 3, 1986—under a Compact of Free Association with the United States. Other neighboring island entities (also former members of the TTPI) also formed constitutional governments, becoming the Republic of the Marshall Islands and the Republic of Palau. The FSM has a seat in the United Nations and has been a member of the Pacific Community since 1983.\n\n","history":"The Federated States of Micronesia are located on the Caroline Islands in the western Pacific Ocean. The history of the modern Federated States of Micronesia is one of settlement by Micronesians; colonization by Spain, Germany, and Japan; United Nations trusteeship under United States-administered Trust Territory of the Pacific Islands; and gradual independence beginning with the ratification of a sovereign constitution in 1979.","historyTitle":"History of Federated States of Micronesia","curated":null,"in